REALROM sample.warn c142 [NesBankingAnalyzer] Bank state becomes unknown here: mechanism write with a genuinely undeterminable value (value recovery could not pin down even one tracked bank bit -- e.g. a load of an unrelated address followed directly by the store, with no AND/ORA immediate to constrain it)
REALROM sample.warn c149 [NesBankingAnalyzer] Bank state becomes unknown here: call to bank-switch helper FUN_c13f, whose latched value is re-derived inside the helper under this call site's registers (no caller argument is consulted), and that derivation did not resolve here
REALROM sample.warn c164 [NesBankingAnalyzer] Bank state becomes unknown here: call to bank-switch helper FUN_c13f, whose latched value is re-derived inside the helper under this call site's registers (no caller argument is consulted), and that derivation did not resolve here
REALROM sample.warn c9c0 [NesBankingAnalyzer] Bank state becomes unknown here: call to bank-switch helper FUN_c139, whose latched value is re-derived inside the helper under this call site's registers (no caller argument is consulted), and that derivation did not resolve here
REALROM sample.note c0d3 [NesBankingAnalyzer] Bank value is RESTORED here, not resolved: this call re-commits the bank READ BACK at c0c1 from bank-identifying ROM byte 8000 -- a byte whose value is the bank it is read from, so the byte read is the bank live at the read, carried on the stack across control flow c0c4..c0d1 -- the save/restore idiom. The bank after this call is whatever 8000 held at that read, not a fresh value this analyzer failed to pin down. A property of the game, not a gap in analysis.
